  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The table ranks the largest federal contracts by total value for FY2027 to date. NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC tops the list with $43.5B in total contract value. LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC follows with $41.6B, and CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC is third with $34.7B. THE BOEING COMPANY holds $22.7B, and HONEYWELL FEDERAL MANUFACTURING & TECHNOLOGIES, LLC and UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC each hold $17.7B. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP shows $15.6B, FLUOR MARINE PROPULSION, LLC shows $15.1B, ALLIANCE FOR ENERGY INNOVATION, LLC shows $11.3B, and MISSION SUPPORT & TEST SERVICES LLC shows $7.7B. The page notes that total award value figures are full contract values, not single-year obligations. Total obligations for FY2027 to date are $43.5B. The ranking highlights large long-term awards to national laboratories, prime defense contractors, and specialized services firms, based on full-contract totals rather than annual spending.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which companies lead the FY2027 list?",
        "body": "NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC leads with $43.5B. LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC and CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC follow with $41.6B and $34.7B respectively. THE BOEING COMPANY, HONEYWELL FEDERAL MANUFACTURING & TECHNOLOGIES, LLC, and UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC round out the top six."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What types of contractors appear in the top ten?",
